        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.142,
            0.925,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "**1. How many different magic squares can be made using the numbers 1 – 9? Ans:** There is exactly one unique magic square with numbers 1 – 9, if we ignore rotations and reflections."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.212,
            0.656,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": "| 8 | 1 | 6 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 | 5 | 7 |\n| 4 | 9 | 2 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_24_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.383,
            0.925,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "**2. Create a magic square using numbers 2 – 10. What strategy would you use for this? Compare it with the magic squares made using 1 – 9. Ans:** We will add 1 to every number in the magic square in Q.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.395,
            0.464,
            0.648,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": "| 9 | 2 | 7 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | 6 | 8 |\n| 5 | 10 | 3 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_24_table_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.636,
            0.431,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": "3. **Take a magic square, and**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.657,
            0.479,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Increase each number by 1**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.678,
            0.421,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Double each number**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.699,
            0.911,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "**In each case, is the resulting grid also a magic square? How do the magic sums change in each case?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
